- Two podman bugs to upstream, both worked around here and both silent:
  `podman machine init --volume src:target:ro` generates a systemd .mount unit
  with no `ro` in Options (podman 5.4, applehv), so the guest mounts it
  read-write and a write reaches the host; and it names the unit after the
  target it was handed without canonicalising it against the machine OS, so a
  target under a symlinked directory produces a unit systemd refuses to mount
  and a machine that comes up without it. Both repros are in the TODO comments
  at host/macos/machine.sh and host/macos/playbook.yaml.

  Work around this, but leave the upstream bug report so we can remove the workaround when it is fixed.

